I've lost 140 HP, AC -20 barbs who were foolish enough to attack a
priest in melee. If you have a wand of sleep and a wand of fire/cold,
you can kill a priest. If you have a good stack of ranged weapons (+4
or better) and can attack the priest out of sight of the watchmen, you
can kill the priest. If you have a wand of polymorph and shock
resistance, you can turn the priest into (any) non-shock resistant
monster, and get him killed by his own deity's lightning.

But if you don't have a good range attack or method such as
cancellation/sleep/paralysis to kill the priest, don't do it.

As for lycanthropy, a lycanthrope must play as if he will polymorph
the next turn. It isn't much fun, because *you can't engrave Elbereth
as a puppyratjackalwolfthing*. Therefore, keep a scroll of scare
monster, or failing that, a scroll of earth in open inventory. When
you polymorph, you can drop the scroll of scare monster or read the
scroll of earth if you're under attack. Furthermore, an uncursed
scroll of earth may do enough damage to immediately revert you, which
is a Good Thing.

The only really Good Thing about lycanthropy is that it provides an
easy means to identify unchanging or polymorph control.

